From fa33bd19014f69149c5f7bf719f3a967ada7787d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lars Grahmann <lars@grahmann.family>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:29:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Support the Kensington VeriMark DT (047d:00f2)

Runs Synaptics' 6.0.11.1132 driver for the VeriMark DT from the Microsoft
Update Catalog instead of Lenovo's 104 build. The DLLs go in
libtudor/verimark/ and are not tracked. Both firmware update entry points
are patched to fail at load time, and a DLL that doesn't match the
expected bytes is refused.

The sensor is USB interface 1 next to a FIDO HID interface, so the first
vendor interface is treated as interface 0 and the HID side stays bound.
The adapter DLL brings its own match-on-chip storage adapter, which is used
when exported: it opens the sensor database by the INF's GUID and its
deletes run DB2_CLEANUP. Enrollments are committed with a payload, which
this driver needs to match against a template.

Fixes in the Windows emulation that the newer driver hit:
TRACE_GUID_REGISTRATION holds a GUID pointer, which broke the stack cookie,
timed waits and joins used relative instead of absolute deadlines, dead
WDF object lists destroyed their head forever, ExitThread unwound through
Windows frames, WMI request callbacks were called with the wrong ABI,
events closed with waiters aborted, and opens with no create handler
never completed. Added CryptoAPI AES encrypt/decrypt and key params,
PROV_RSA_FULL, CryptAcquireContextW, security descriptor and hidden
window stubs, power and session notification stubs, a few WDF functions,
memoryless control transfers, and WPP trace output for unknown messages
with -t.
